{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","id":"pg_6ac5270e789b524da49b5b1e094e0acb","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gi-dellav-zerostack-docs-robots-txt-efd142b3ac46-5b1e094e0acb.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9bb8a7f8c2f653dd933860365ad07bec"],"title":"gi-dellav/zerostack/docs/robots.txt @ efd142b3ac46","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_b6c32da7e15bddec977fc3a7741224fbfd94c968c01b9526dd2145d39c19ee2f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent automatically loads AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md from the project root or ancestor directories into the system prompt, and optionally ARCHITECTURE.md under the archmd feature; -n disables context-file loading."}],"claim_ids":["clm_b6c32da7e15bddec977fc3a7741224fbfd94c968c01b9526dd2145d39c19ee2f"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","id":"pg_95fc1064401655f89e5eef168fe1993f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gi-dellav-zerostack-docs-architecture-md-efd142b3ac46-ef168fe1993f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6a0ec939534d55fb9145855ee386d0f2"],"title":"gi-dellav/zerostack/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md @ efd142b3ac46","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2621f57e5e543ed6333145b2ac1421c16846c8bb4a02f5919691ed5acc9397b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"zerostack is a minimal coding agent written in Rust, inspired by pi and opencode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2e0f53730c6600e81363071e70dcfd9892eceae517417fa72b8b6f97c5ccbb39"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Windows support is untested, and the loop and git-worktree features are explicitly marked experimental."},{"claim_ids":["clm_306860977918cce409e21758b1b7a17340a36c7a785fcaf9875ad3835445592b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The gated memory feature keeps plain-Markdown notes (global MEMORY.md plus per-project logs) injected into the system prompt each session; it is not in the default build."},{"claim_ids":["clm_37b0a4f25d1aeaebaec119c597b8ef81651b754990e4e8ca0b8d516104bd262b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"With the acp feature, zerostack acts as an ACP (JSON-RPC) agent server over stdio or TCP so editors like Zed can connect; ACP is not in the default build."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f72a61abe0f3a003d982e22d44f8b8b41ad0b184cd8aabb9ac65a137376ea4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Optional --sandbox mode runs bash commands in bubblewrap (or zerobox on macOS), masks credential directories by default, and can require the backend via --sandbox-required; network stays on unless disabled."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4256c5f6432f8b6d742c10ed42857034047becc61bcd039200b6a0db939717d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets users wanting a lightweight terminal coding agent, citing ~30k LoC, a 26MB binary, and roughly 16MB average RAM versus much heavier JS-based agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_70e6634cb4583ca020b9a5ffbe32929409d6431e540997ec6a1bc8bc483d079b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"There are five permission modes (restrictive, readonly, guarded, standard, yolo) with per-tool glob patterns, session allowlists, and doom-loop detection for repeated identical tool calls."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7ae34aa3c592b144e7522469a29ee2ccd1ec4888ae939185cf8bff32600a937c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A prompts system lets users switch built-in system prompts (code, plan, review, debug, ask, etc.) at runtime via /prompt, and custom prompts can be added as markdown files under the config prompts directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_863568697c6018c7031fe8170fda8ad8cc16ec2284e1235912a0cd1487fce507"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Git worktree integration offers /worktree, /wt-merge, and /wt-exit slash commands for a branch-per-task workflow, with optional auto-merge on exit; the feature is labeled experimental."},{"claim_ids":["clm_99ae4ebf9a0c929a178f2b2f2ec7bc5c3d90e96c7c94d0b7aedbee71df455c15"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions are saved as JSON under $XDG_DATA_HOME/zerostack/sessions/ and can be resumed with -c, -r, or --session <id>; auto-compaction summarizes old messages near the context-window limit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2b75a0e028c8e9f9f14e85445c1c8bf8269f291b6c5b0bc5a9af8127dd4a72d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An iterative loop system (experimental) repeatedly works through a LOOP_PLAN.md plan with validation commands, usable via /loop in the TUI or headless flags like --loop-prompt and --loop-max."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b016ef0a48afc385263a6b721486f701384c7e16606d662d3a5bb7e6acecc293"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A --dangerously-skip-permissions flag bypasses all permission checks entirely and is not a runtime-toggleable mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6c32da7e15bddec977fc3a7741224fbfd94c968c01b9526dd2145d39c19ee2f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent automatically loads AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md from the project root or ancestor directories into the system prompt, and optionally ARCHITECTURE.md under the archmd feature; -n disables context-file loading."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f224932fef0a847358ad28ff5b2ab417f26566b29c17c686ca2539a8541e2708"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent supports multiple LLM providers: OpenRouter (default), OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, Gemini, and Ollama, plus custom providers configured via config.yaml."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2621f57e5e543ed6333145b2ac1421c16846c8bb4a02f5919691ed5acc9397b9","clm_2e0f53730c6600e81363071e70dcfd9892eceae517417fa72b8b6f97c5ccbb39","clm_306860977918cce409e21758b1b7a17340a36c7a785fcaf9875ad3835445592b","clm_37b0a4f25d1aeaebaec119c597b8ef81651b754990e4e8ca0b8d516104bd262b","clm_3f72a61abe0f3a003d982e22d44f8b8b41ad0b184cd8aabb9ac65a137376ea4f","clm_4256c5f6432f8b6d742c10ed42857034047becc61bcd039200b6a0db939717d8","clm_70e6634cb4583ca020b9a5ffbe32929409d6431e540997ec6a1bc8bc483d079b","clm_7ae34aa3c592b144e7522469a29ee2ccd1ec4888ae939185cf8bff32600a937c","clm_863568697c6018c7031fe8170fda8ad8cc16ec2284e1235912a0cd1487fce507","clm_99ae4ebf9a0c929a178f2b2f2ec7bc5c3d90e96c7c94d0b7aedbee71df455c15","clm_a2b75a0e028c8e9f9f14e85445c1c8bf8269f291b6c5b0bc5a9af8127dd4a72d","clm_b016ef0a48afc385263a6b721486f701384c7e16606d662d3a5bb7e6acecc293","clm_b6c32da7e15bddec977fc3a7741224fbfd94c968c01b9526dd2145d39c19ee2f","clm_f224932fef0a847358ad28ff5b2ab417f26566b29c17c686ca2539a8541e2708"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","id":"pg_97ae7ff4c2bc54af8dccc7d38736a97a","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gi-dellav-zerostack-readme-md-efd142b3ac46-c7d38736a97a.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"title":"gi-dellav/zerostack/README.md @ efd142b3ac46","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
